PS5: HDR at 10/12 bpc, RGB range and 4K over FRL on VERDE (opt-in, all off by default); VRR switch experimental

The VERDE side of the official ps5-linux-patches b33e7c5 (#81), "ps5: add opt-in hdr, deep colour, frl, vrr and allm
on verde", on our display stack instead of the official HDMI plan:

  the verde hdmi bridge only gets the 8 bpc tmds set-up, an avi for 1080p60, 1440p and 4k60 and no hdr signalling.
  sony uses the same bridge for frl, deep colour, vrr and allm. [...] not tested on a verde console. the messages
  were compared byte for byte with ps5 os captures from two verde consoles

Switches (drivers/ps5/hdmi.c), every one off by default; with all of them off VERDE gets exactly the writes it got
before (same register sequence, the AVI byte for byte for all 256 VICs) and FLAVA3 is unchanged:
- hdmi.verde_infoframes (live): the official verde_avi/verde_packets/verde_if_update InfoFrames (AVI with the
  stream's format, BT.2020 and RGB range from hdmi.rgb_range; the DRM InfoFrame for HDR). The HDR Static Metadata
  block is kept in the EDID only with it on (verde_drop_hdr() otherwise, as since v2.9), and isHdmiHdrSupported()
  is true on VERDE with it.
- hdmi.verde_avi_game (live, default on): IT content and content type game in the AVI, what Bazzite always sent;
  off sends the official AVI without them.
- hdmi.verde_deep_colour: HDR never goes out at 8 bpc. Over TMDS (1440p120, 2160p60 and below) HDR is 12 bpc
  YCbCr 4:2:2, the same TMDS clock as 8 bpc RGB (the official dm_ps5_set_hdr_timing() rule). The RGB 10/12 bpc
  path (official ps5_hdmi_bpc_limit(), depth in 0x3033) is in but does not run today: ps5-display.patch holds
  every PS5 connector's max_requested_bpc at 8 (drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic.c, "Deeper RGB comes out of the
  bridges as posterized contours"), so SDR stays 8 bpc RGB, as before.
- hdmi.verde_frl: 2160p100/120 over HDMI 2.1 FRL in YCbCr 4:2:2 with the official VERDE sequences (0x84 and 0x8a
  registered with the bridge firmware, then 5/3 02); with HDR at 10 bpc, the most the HBR3 x4 link carries in
  4:2:2 (12 does not fit; the official planner picks the same), SDR at 8. No 6 bpc on that output. Our addition:
  VERDE has no 0x7019, so the link counts as up on the bridge's "link / picture up" notification (0x03); without it
  in frl_check_fn's window the display is marked failed and amdgpu falls back, as on FLAVA3. The HDR InfoFrame is
  written again after link up, since sequence 0x8a rewrites the AVI and packet enables. 2160p60 RGB deeper than 8
  bpc over FRL is in for the same future as the RGB path above.
- hdmi.verde_vrr (experimental, do not turn on yet): the official verde_vrr (0x8000 bit 7, 0x9200, 0x3271/0x326a,
  0x3261/0x3262 in the TMDS setup and in FRL sequence 0x8a; modes as the official vrr_mode_ok(), including the two
  1440p timings with Sony's 1440p fields in the timing SDP; SDP and ignore-MSA as the official policy). The
  register writes match the official byte for byte, and it fails on the one TV tried (below).
Not ported: ALLM on VERDE.

Seen here on a PS5 Slim CFI-2115 (VERDE, system software 13.60) with an LG C6, kernel 7.3.3-viva of v2.10 with
this patch (bzImage and amdgpu.ko swapped; Module.symvers: 0 CRCs changed), switches on the command line,
16 November (dmesg lines from drivers/ps5/hdmi.c):
- 1440p120 HDR: "setup: 2560x1440@120 497750 kHz vic 0, 12 bpc YCbCr 4:2:2"; the TV reports HDR.
- 2160p60 HDR: "setup: 3840x2160@60 594000 kHz vic 97, 12 bpc YCbCr 4:2:2"; games at 60 fps. 2160p60 itself
  needs none of the switches (Game Mode had been pinned to 1440p120 on this console).
- 2160p120 HDR: "setup: 3840x2160@120 1188000 kHz vic 118, 10 bpc YCbCr 4:2:2", "over VERDE FRL (VIC 118,
  format 2, 10-bit)", "VERDE FRL link up (bridge notification 0x03)"; the TV's game bar shows 3840x2160, 120 Hz
  and HDR; Dusklight and Forza Horizon 2 played at 2160p120. Both 2160p rates chosen from Steam's display
  settings.
- EDID announces and re-arms per start: 2 and 2 on the first, 1 and 0 on the last; Dolby Digital 5.1 over HDMI
  unchanged.
- VRR (hdmi.verde_vrr=1): at 1440p120 (TMDS) and at 2160p120 (FRL) the TV drops the link (bridge notification
  0x01) about 2 s after every VRR setup and announces its EDID again, never 0x03. Over FRL the link check marks
  VRR failed and the display comes back at fixed refresh after 17 s; over TMDS there is no such check, the
  re-arms run out (4 in 120 s) and the screen stays black until VRR is switched off. Not tried: SDR, RGB.
- Starts: five with these builds. Two, back to back, stopped before any picture (white light, no signal, no
  journal); the same build started normally the next time, with a network console that the two stops did not
  have. The other three were normal. Cause not found.
